PART 5. TEST FIXTURES AND DATA (testdata/)
------------------------------------------

Nothing under testdata/ is compiled into the library or the vega2svg binary.
The Go toolchain ignores directories named testdata, and no go:embed
directive refers to them. These files matter only if you redistribute the
repository itself.

  testdata/bar.vg.json
    Adapted from the Vega "Bar Chart" gallery example (UW IDL,
    BSD-3-Clause).
  testdata/timeseries.vg.json, testdata/aggregate.vg.json
    Written for this project.
  testdata/*.svg
    Output generated by this library from the specs above.

  testdata/examples/*.vg.json  (76 specs)
    The Vega example gallery, downloaded from
    https://vega.github.io/vega/examples/<name>.vg.json. These are the
    published copies of the specs in the vega/vega GitHub repository and
    are under its BSD-3-Clause license (UW IDL). Unmodified.

  testdata/examples-lite/*.vl.json  (54 specs)
    The Vega-Lite example gallery, downloaded from
    https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/examples/<name>.vl.json. These are the
    published copies of the specs in the vega/vega-lite GitHub repository
    and are under its BSD-3-Clause license (UW IDL). Unmodified.

  testdata/examples/data/ and testdata/examples-lite/data/
    Downloaded from https://vega.github.io/vega/data/ and
    https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/data/. Both serve the vega-datasets
    collection (https://github.com/vega/vega-datasets). The vega-datasets
    package as a whole is BSD-3-Clause, but its datapackage.json records a
    separate original source and license for each file. Those per-file
    records are reproduced below exactly as vega-datasets states them; they
    have not been independently verified. Unmodified.

    Notes on the per-file terms:
      * CC-BY-4.0 requires attribution to the listed source when the data
        is redistributed.
      * OGL-UK-3.0 (UK Open Government Licence) requires an attribution
        statement such as "Contains public sector information licensed
        under the Open Government Licence v3.0".
      * ODbL-1.0 (londonTubeLines.json, OpenStreetMap-derived) requires
        attribution and is share-alike for the database itself. It does not
        extend to code that merely reads the data.
      * "not specified" means vega-datasets records no license. Those files
        carry no explicit grant beyond the vega-datasets package license.
        If that matters for your use, delete them and the specs that use
        them; the gallery tests would then need those cases removed.


